The purpose of the code is to return a list of the
digits of the next largest palindromic number given
a list of single-digit integers representing a
palindromic number. Translating this was thankfully
not as hard as I thought. This was translated from a
SoftDes assignment written in python, and the similarities
between the languages definitely made themselves clear.
It was a bit hard for me to completely translate it
though because I couldn't even remember how the
code worked originally, so I had to think back on how
the Python worked to find the respective commands or
functions in Kotlin. I'm doing this right after
having taken notes on Kotlin, so a lot of the concepts
especially regarding collections and how to reference
their aspects was still fresh in my mind.